{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/2452","id":5346426401,"node_id":"PR_kwDOTIDrTc8AAAABPqv-IQ","html_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2452","diff_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2452.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2452.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/2452","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/2452/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/2452/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/issues/2452/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/statuses/4a5bbebdb2d2ea7217f7b44a36a94e398146f5e9","number":2452,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(sync): preserve pending agent mail and cancel reserved wakes (D659–D664)","user":{"login":"IridiumMaster","id":4607679,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MDc2Nzk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4607679?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster","html_url":"https://github.com/IridiumMaster","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/IridiumMaster/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"A lasting turn error can repeatedly restart pending agent mail without saving it (#2443). Accepted D659–D664 now persist pending input after terminal errors, save unanswered mail for the next explicit turn, allow idle children with queued mail to release capacity with durable/volatile handback, and reserve wakes before refusal discovery so Interrupt can cancel them. Pre-turn kill-switch/sign-in refusals retain their behavior. Tests retain no-preemption and full parent-history forks.\n\nBounded reliability fixes authorized by Travis on 2026-11-16. Product specification: **Shipping MVP — LIVE**, Agent orchestration: “durable mailboxes, supervision, resume, and recovery.”\n\nRust 1.99.1: scoped core clippy fix and changed-file formatting passed; final build passed. Core all on `4a5bbebdb2d2ea7217f7b44a36a94e398146f5e9`: **3,106 passed / 83 failed**, versus baseline **3,082/106** (+24/-23). Twenty baseline failure names now pass; four renamed parameter suffixes are reported separately rather than credited. The one newly failing MCP startup-cache case passed a separate focused rerun (1/0); its full-run log showed tracing-subscriber panics in SQLite workers before an event timeout. All decision-specific core integration cases pass, including six terminal-error cases, 13 retained no-preemption cases, four full-history cases, durable eviction and Interrupt/refusal ordering.\n\nFull library/app runs on the same production changes (later commits change core tests only): core lib **4,840/4**, app lib **464/0**, app suite **1,714/12**, versus app baseline **1,710/15** (+4/-3). Three added D660/refusal units pass separately on the final head. Core/app CLI exclusions remain 24/13. The app suite's one new path-decoding failure passes a separate short-temp-alias rerun (1/0); full and focused counts remain separate. The existing app eviction failure filters typed agent messages while its mock provider emits user messages; captured events show both notes delivered, but this failed app assertion does not establish provider-request exactly-once counts. Separate new core eviction regressions cover retention, order and exactly-once consumption.\n\nIndependent read-only Opus 5.5 High final round **2/2 APPROVE**, with **D663 SECURITY: PASS**, on exact head `4a5bbebdb2d2ea7217f7b44a36a94e398146f5e9`. [Exact-head corbanu-security approval](https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2452#pullrequestreview-5929887951). Merged after all21 checks completed (10 documented sync-base failures,5success,6skip). [Every red has final-head log evidence for the existing CLI conflict/fmt blocker (#2274)](https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/pull/2452#issuecomment-6933226517).\n\nCoordinated with main merge #8 (#2450), now merged with no changed-file overlap; no base merge needed. Related main port #2453 and small sync decisions #2454. #2443 remains open until their outcomes are recorded.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-16T22:33:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-17T00:03:39Z","closed_at":"2026-11-17T00:01:28Z","merged_at":"2026-11-17T00:03:11Z","merge_commit_sha":"b6f84e1817aace7efa685bd53a7e7b4c99655256","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"CorbanuCore:work/astra-d659-sync","ref":"work/astra-d659-sync","repo":{"id":1283517261,"node_id":"R_kgDOTIDrTQ","name":"CorbanuTerminal","full_name":"CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal","owner":{"login":"CorbanuCore","id":315989408,"node_id":"O_kgDOEtWdoA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/315989408?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore","html_url":"https://github.com/CorbanuCore","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCore/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CorbanuCor